Package: wb-node-red
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 nodejs,
 adduser
Recommends: nginx, mosquitto, wb-mqtt-homeui (>= 2.235.4)
Description: Node-RED for Wiren Board controllers (native)
 Runs Node-RED natively on the controller host as a systemd service, with the
 Wiren Board palette (node-red-contrib-wirenboard) and a default flow pre-wired
 to the local MQTT broker on localhost:1883 and the device tree (/devices/#).
 .
 Node-RED and the palette are vendored into the package at build time, so no
 npm download or native compilation happens on the controller; Node.js comes
 from the distribution (Depends: nodejs) so its security updates flow from the
 Wiren Board / Debian repository.
 .
 The service runs as a dedicated unprivileged user with the editor bound to
 loopback and reverse-proxied on a dedicated HTTPS port (21880) behind the homeui
 login (admin only); the old /node-red/ path is kept as a redirect to that port.
 User data and the runtime tree persist under /mnt/data across upgrades and
 updates are explicit (the package is excluded from unattended-upgrades).
